From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:31:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE, one dispatch with its inputs for
 replay

NVK_DISPATCH_PROFILE names the compute shaders that take the time, but
timing NAK's code against another driver's with synthetic inputs misleads:
real data drives loops differently.  NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE=<hash>[,<hash>...]
captures one dispatch of each listed compute shader (vk_shader::src_hash,
vkd3d-proton's DXIL hash as in NVK_DISPATCH_PROFILE) with everything a
standalone program needs to run it again on the same data: the SPIR-V, the
push constants, the grid and the contents of every descriptor and root
buffer address the shader reads.

When a compute pipeline of a listed shader is created, the common pipeline
code hands its SPIR-V and pipeline layout to the driver
(vk_device::compute_spirv_hook).  NVK scans it: the push constant block,
the resource variables (set, binding, descriptor type, writable or not),
the array index of every descriptor access that is a push constant word
plus a constant or a constant (how vkd3d-proton indexes its heaps from root
table offsets), and every buffer device address loaded from a push constant
(vkd3d-proton's root descriptors), with the pointee's size.  Other index
expressions are listed as unsupported.

When such a dispatch is recorded (direct or indirect, after
NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_DELAY_S, default 20 s, once NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_TRIGGER
exists if set, after NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_SKIP matching dispatches,
NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_COUNT per shader), each referenced descriptor is read
from its set's CPU map or a mapped descriptor buffer and mapped back to its
image view, buffer view, sampler or buffer range through tables kept from
view and sampler creation (and the EDB buffer view cache).  Copy engine
copies of each view's subresources, of the buffer ranges, of the root
buffers (to the end of their allocation or the pointee's size), and of
indirect arguments go into a GART staging buffer behind a flush and wait
for idle, right before the launch; with NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_POST=1 the
writable resources are copied again after it.  A copy engine semaphore marks
the end.  When the command buffer is reset or destroyed, a capture whose
marker landed is written to NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_DIR (default
%ProgramData%\Helios\dcap): <hash>-p<pid>-<n>\manifest.json, shader.spv,
push.bin and one raw file per resource.  Events go to mesa_logi and
nvk-dcap.log in that directory.

Limits: no device-generated commands; single-plane, single-sample,
non-sparse-residency images (color, or one aspect of a depth view);
descriptors as the CPU sees them when the dispatch is recorded; root
addresses of unsized pointees are copied up to 16 MiB; an image two
descriptors alias is captured twice.  A capturing command buffer of the
async compute family runs on the channel with every engine.
---
